lic remodeling of the hair follicle immune system in mice. <source>J. Invest. Dermatol.</source> <volume>111</volume>:<fpage>7</fpage>&#x02013;18.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9665380</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Sayama, K., Y. Hanakawa, Y. Shirakata, K. Yamasaki, Y. Sawada, L. Sun, K. Yamanishi, H. Ichijo, and K. Hashimoto. <year>2001</year>. Apoptosis signal-regulating kinase 1 (ASK1) is an intracellular inducer of keratinocyte differentiation. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>276</volume>:<fpage>999</fpage>&#x02013;1004.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11029458</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Sayama, K., H. Komatsuzawa, K. Yamasaki, Y. Shirakata, Y. Hanakawa, K. Ouhara, S. Tokumaru, X. Dai, M. Tohyama, P. Ten Dijke, et al. <year>2005</year>. New mechanisms of skin innate immunity: ASK1-mediated keratinocyte differentiation regulates the expression of beta-defensins, LL37, and TLR2. <source>Eur. J. Immunol.</source> <volume>35</volume>:<fpage>1886</fpage>&#x02013;1895.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15864780</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Sekine, Y., K. Takeda, and H. Ichijo. <year>2006</year>. The ASK1-MAP kinase signaling in ER stress and neurodegenerative diseases. <source>Curr. Mol. Med.</source> <volume>6</volume>:<fpage>87</fpage>&#x02013;97.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16472116</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Stenn, K.S., and R. Paus. <year>2001</year>. Controls of hair follicle cycling. <source>Physiol. Rev.</source> <volume>81</volume>:<fpage>449</fpage>&#x02013;494.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11152763</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Taylor, G., M.S. Lehrer, P.J. Jensen, T.T. Sun, and R.M. Lavker. <year>2000</year>. Involvement of follicular stem cells in forming not only the follicle but also the epidermis. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>102</volume